# a5d715a added `asserts_code_behaviour`, the promote-direction fail-safe that
# says a finding asserting what the CODE does is not confined to comment prose,
# so no comment-prose refusal may fire against it however its wording reads. It
# was wired into `_observation_refusal`, which only `foundry_add_defect` calls.
# Its own docstring names a second consumer and the reason for the export:
# "Exported because `foundry_sync_defects`'s auto-demotion branch faces the
# mirror of the same question and must not re-derive an answer to it."
#
# That wiring was never made. `find_referencing_symbols` returned exactly one
# call site, in tools/foundry.py, and the symbol appeared nowhere in
# foundry_orchestrator.py. Sync's demotion branch still ran the two-guard shape
# that was insufficient before a5d715a: `record_denylist_tripwire`, then
# `observation_class`.
#
# The first block below is that disagreement, driven live. The finding is the
# NO_SECURITY_VOCABULARY fixture the observation tests added specifically to
# prove the fail-safe is STRUCTURAL: it carries no security vocabulary, so no
# widening of vocab's never-demote denylist can ever reach it, and its prose
# classifies as DIRECTION_WORD. Before the fix the two doors answered
# differently -- `foundry_add_defect` filed it as D-001, `foundry_sync_defects`
# returned {"added": 0, "observations": 1} with defects.json left empty and
# observations.json's `tripwire` also empty, since no denylist entry matches it.
# A stream that happened to file through the batch door lost a real defect and
# was told ok:true. Both lines now read True.
#
# The guard is placed where the promote path places it -- AFTER the denylist
# (so a denylisted finding still trips the audit signal D-036 wired) and BEFORE
# the observation class (so a behavioural claim is never demoted on the strength
# of its prose). It is IMPORTED from tools/foundry.py, never re-derived: a
# fail-safe with two copies is a fail-safe that drifts, and the disagreement
# above is exactly what that costs.
#
# The second block is the regression coverage the defect named as missing. No
# test drove the SECURITY_BATTERY or NO_SECURITY_VOCABULARY fixtures through
# `foundry_sync_defects` at all, so the gap had no pin either. The corpus is
# IMPORTED from the tests that pin the other door rather than restated, because
# a parity test owning its own copy would keep passing while the two corpora
# drifted -- the shape of the bug it exists to catch.
#
# `test_the_two_filing_paths_agree_on_what_a_defect_is` is the derived-membership
# pin. It asserts an OUTCOME (did this reach the defect ledger?) and never a
# mechanism: the doors legitimately differ in HOW they decline -- Sync
# auto-demotes to the observations ledger, Foundry-Defect returns a named
# refusal telling the caller to re-file -- and pinning which guard admitted a
# finding would pass for the wrong reason the moment either half moved. The
# four `prose-*` rows carry the other direction: parity has to hold at "not a
# defect" too, or a guard that matched everything would satisfy the battery
# while quietly deleting the observation channel AC-001 exists to fill.
#
# Run against the pre-fix tree, `no-security-vocabulary` fails with the message
# the assertion is written to produce: "the filing paths disagree: Foundry-Sync
# declined this finding, Foundry-Defect kept it". The ten battery rows pass
# without the fix -- the denylist rescues those on its own -- which is why the
# fixture with no security noun in it is the one that makes the pin structural.
